WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.240
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.150
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.900
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.600
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.700
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.070
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:46.000
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.250
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.520
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:06.260
What is truly precious?

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.920
Showdown!
Dungeon Dice Monsters

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.480
You agreed without knowing the game rules.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.970
Yugi, your days as a duelist will be over today!

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.060
Set up the DDM Ring!

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.100
What's this?

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:04.400
I've reconfigured the Duel Monsters virtual ring to use it for DDM.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.170
Shall we begin?

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.710
These dice are used in the game.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:20.220
A player selects 15 of these dice.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:26.890
I've already selected my dice pool, so choose whatever dice you like.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.080
These dice have different colors and icons.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.430
Which ones should I choose?

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.830
What's wrong?  Are you scared?

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.340
I made my selection!

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:43.160
The game will take place on the Dark Field, a dark underground land.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.580
Place all your selected dice into the shooter.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.490
DDM...  What kind of game is this?

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.620
Your dice have returned.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.360
They've been shuffled fairly.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:07.370
The dice order is an important factor in deciding the outcome of the game.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.730
We each take three dice.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:16.870
We're Dungeon Masters on this field.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.480
Each Dungeon Master has three life points.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.320
In other words, you lose if you're attacked three times.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.450
Start the game!

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.450
He's playing a game that he know nothing about!

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.360
He's played into Otogi's hands!

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:35.930
Hooray hooray Otogi!

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.430
Thank you.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.450
Otogi!

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.100
What a stuck-up punk!

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.960
Dogs can't talk!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.550
I'll go first.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.980
The player rolls three dice on his turn.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.620
Two of the crests match.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:07.180
The icons on the dice are known as crests.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.360
The star-shaped crest is a Summon Crest.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:18.270
If at least two of the three dice show a Summon Crest, you're allowed to summon a monster.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.170
Summon a monster?

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:25.250
You can place one of the matching dice on the field.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.250
Set up the white die!

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.600
Dimension Dice!

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.360
Ryu-Kishin!

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.360
There's a monster inside the die?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:45.530
The die opened up, creating a dungeon path.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:52.450
DDM is a strategic game where you use dice to expand your dungeon and conquer your enemy's territory.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:57.540
The player transforms his dice into a dungeon on the field.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:04.580
You use your summoned monsters to move into your opponent's territory and win by defeating your opponent.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.140
I see.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:11.220
Summoned monsters can only move through the dungeon created by the dice.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:17.230
Whoever uses more dice to spread his dungeon will have an advantage in the game.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.360
This is an excellent game!

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.100
Yugi, it's your turn.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:29.510
Otogi, don't forget that if I win this game, you have to free Jonouchi!

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.010
If you can defeat me, that is.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:34.000
I'm counting on you, Yugi!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.570
I believe that you'll win!

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.450
No talking, dog!

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.880
Yugi can do it!

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:45.320
Yeah, he'll come through to defend our friendship.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.830
It's impossible for you to win this game.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.300
Dice roll!

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.900
None of the crests match!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.920
You've failed to summon.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:04.720
Since you chose dice with high Levels, they're hard to summon.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:21.060
There are six types of crests on the dice: Summon, Movement, Magic, Attack, Defense and Trap.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:27.430
The Ryu-kishin die has three Summon Crests, making it easy to summon.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:31.670
But since it's easier to summon, its Level is lower.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:35.170
Look at the dice you have.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.110
These dice only have one Summon Crest.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:44.720
Correct.  The fewer the Summon Crests, the harder it is to summon.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:48.180
But in exchange, the monster's Level is higher.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:54.190
The number of monsters you summon is a deciding factor on the outcome of this game.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:58.680
If you only choose high Level dice, you can't win.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.690
Oh no!  I chose dice whose Levels are all too high!

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.550
That's not fair, Otogi!

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:08.610
You should've told him before starting the game!

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:11.820
It's impossible to win under these conditions!

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.440
Restart the game!

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:15.770
It's too late to stop the game.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.420
Okay, Yugi?

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:18.850
It's my turn.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.790
Dice roll!

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.790
Good.  I rolled two Summon Crests.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:33.800
I can choose one of the two and summon the monster.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.800
Dimension Dice!

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.140
I summon Yaranzo!

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.960
He's building his dungeon towards my territory.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:53.480
You must place your dice so that the dungeon remains connected.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:58.530
Since I also rolled a Movement Crest, I move my monster one space forward.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:04.510
Non-Summon Crests are stocked in your crest pool.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.400
It's your turn.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.110
Dice roll!

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.240
It's no good.  They didn't match again.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:18.740
If you don't summon a monster soon, you can't stop my monsters from advancing on you.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.400
My turn.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.540
Dice roll!

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.310
Another match.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.090
Dimension Dice!

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.310
Gator Dragon!

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.400
Move one space forward!

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:40.630
Dice roll!

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.630
All right!  Two of my dice match!

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:46.300
I can summon!

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.760
Look closer.  You can't summon unless the stars are the same Level.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:53.660
What?

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.050
My turn.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.550
Level 4 dice...

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.050
It's going so well that it's no fun.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:01.550
I'll play around a bit.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.120
Dice roll!

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:12.440
Wonderful!  The goddess of DDM is smiling on me today.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.030
I successfully summon!

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.670
What is that?

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:24.200
I'll save the surprise for later.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.070
It's your turn.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:27.580
Dice roll!

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.080
I just can't get a match!

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:36.450
I heard rumors about your gaming skills, but they're nothing special.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.520
But it's still too early for you to regret challenging me.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.460
The fun of DDM is only getting started.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:44.960
Dice roll!

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:51.620
With these dice, I'm in control of your territory!

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.200
Dimension Dice!

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.240
I summon The 13th Grave!

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:03.710
With three more squares, he can attack me.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:11.050
If I don't get Summon Crests next turn, it'll be difficult to stop his advance.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:14.060
What's wrong?  It's your turn.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:17.420
But no matter how many times you try, it's pointless.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:21.460
With those dice, the odds of summoning a monster are too low.

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:28.570
Like he said, Level 4 dice only have one Summon Crest.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.000
But I must make a match!

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:32.620
Dice roll!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.630
All right!  I have two Summon Crests!

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:57.220
What?  He matched up two Summon Crests using Level 4 dice?

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.270
Dimension Dice!

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:08.310
I summon Level 4 Mighty Mage!

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.510
I activate my crest I have in stock!

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:15.080
Move forward and launch a magical attack on The 13th Grave!

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:19.420
Lightning Rod!

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:22.680
He did it!

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:23.560
Yugi!

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:24.760
All right!

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:31.630
Since he rolled a Magic Crest with his Summon Crests, he could do a magical attack.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.540
Otogi, this match is only getting started!

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:02.000
Yeah!  He managed to summon a monster!

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:05.220
Will that stop Yugi from being attacked?

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.500
Look at that.

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:14.510
Otogi's dice dungeon has stretched into Yugi's territory, and he also has many more monsters.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:22.240
Can you defend against so many monsters with just one Mighty Mage?

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:23.250
Here I go.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.300
Dice roll!

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:30.670
Good.  I matched my Summon Crests.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:33.830
Dimension Dice!

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.000
I summon Blast Lizard!

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:44.780
Blast Lizard's Level and attack points are low.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:50.750
But if I use a Magic Crest, it can destroy high Level monsters with its bombs.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:53.000
So it has a special effect.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:57.200
If I don't get more defenders, I won't have enough to stop his attacks.

00:12:57.650 --> 00:12:58.750
My turn!

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:02.490
These dice have three Summon Crests.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.120
I can summon a monster easily.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:06.760
Dice roll!

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:10.300
Good!  I can summon!

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:11.930
Dimension Dice!

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:19.940
I summon Winged Dragon, Guardian of the Fortress #1!

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:23.180
It strengthens my defenses!

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.180
I'm not sure about that.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.450
My turn!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:28.850
Dice roll!

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:33.260
You can't summon.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:37.860
You still don't know how deep this game is.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:44.360
By combining dice crests in different ways, all sorts of combo attacks are possible.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:47.370
What?  There are combo attacks?

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:53.520
By comboing the abilities of different crests, you can draw out a monster's effects.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.240
In this game, that's called a “combo attack.”

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.820
First, I use a Movement Crest to move my Blast Lizard.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:06.120
Then I'll use four Magic Crests to allow it to attack a Level 2 monster.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:18.470
After going through the trouble of summoning it, Yugi.  Too bad.

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.470
Otogi, you're so cool!

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:23.470
Yugi...

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:26.470
It's my turn.

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:27.610
Dice roll!

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:31.380
I can't summon.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.710
My turn.  Dice roll!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:39.150
I summon Level 3 Dark Assailant.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.730
And I activate a Movement Crest.

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:52.270
Monsters, advance!

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:05.650
It's your turn to roll the dice, or will you give up?

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:11.750
It'll take a miracle to defeat me because I invented this game.

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:15.320
What?  Otogi, you invented this game?

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:25.550
Yes.  The world should've known me by now as the inventor and first champion of Dungeon Dice Monsters.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:33.950
Yugi, I know that you defeated Pegasus, the inventor and champion of Duel Monsters, at Duelist Kingdom.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:41.040
But you didn't know that while you gained glory, you crushed my dreams.

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:42.320
What?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.580
Dungeon Dice Monsters...

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:53.560
I put all my ideas into this game to create my masterpiece.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:16:02.070
To spread Dungeon Dice Monsters worldwide, I emailed my business plan to Pegasus's homepage.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:05.280
Several days later...

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:12.400
Pegasus sent me an email saying that he read my business plan.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:19.350
Hello, Otogi boy!

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:24.550
He said that he wanted to meet me in person.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:32.220
Full of excitement, I went to Pegasus's Duelist Kingdom.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:52.220
Within a short period of time, Pegasus had modified Dungeon Dice Monsters into a perfect game.

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:59.720
And even though it was his first match, he defeated me - the inventor of the game.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.400
I win.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.070
Incredible.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:14.240
Otogi boy, your Dungeon Dice Monsters is a wonderful game.

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:19.600
Let's popularize this game around the world together.

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:21.650
Thank you very much.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:34.520
We promised to finalize the contracts after the Duelist Kingdom tournament was over.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:44.430
But after losing to you at Duelist Kingdom, I haven't been able to contact Pegasus.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:50.240
Yugi Muto, you destroyed my plan to spread DDM throughout the world!

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.250
I didn't know anything about this.

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:55.610
Since I've now battled you, I know for sure.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:18:00.080
There's no way a perfect champion like Pegasus would lose against you!

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:02.730
You cheated to defeat Pegasus!

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:04.460
You're wrong, Otogi!

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:05.610
I don't believe you!

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:09.510
No matter what I say, you won't believe me.

00:18:09.510 --> 00:18:13.820
Don't forget the condition that you can never play Duel Monsters again!

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:17.020
I'm getting revenge for Pegasus!

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:19.170
It's my turn!

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:20.710
Dice roll!

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:23.610
Good!

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:26.180
I've matched two Summon Crests!

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.910
I'm counting on this one!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:29.680
Dimension Dice!

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:38.090
I summon Thunder Ball!

00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:43.710
It's a Level 3 monster, but its stats are only 10.

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:46.000
It's no match for my monsters!

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:51.000
But it's a troublesome monster if he has crests that will let him use its effect.

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:54.170
My turn.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:19:00.510
Good.  I rolled Movement and Attack Crests.

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:04.400
I move Blast Lizard and Gator Dragon.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:07.190
Oh no!

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:09.960
Gator Dragon has reached Yugi!

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:12.690
This is bad.  What's going to happen?

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:23.310
Here I go!  Gator Dragon attacks!

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:25.570
Dragon Fire!

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:38.080
Otogi, you're incredible!

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:43.940
Damn!  Yugi lost one of his heart marks!

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:46.760
What are you doing?

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.630
You only have two life left.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:56.470
Someone who cheated to defeat Pegasus can't win Dungeon Dice Monsters!

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:57.700
Cheat?

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:01.400
I'll never let you play Duel Monsters again.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:03.020
I hope you're prepared!

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:10.220
I won't let him tarnish the Duel Monsters glory that my other self and I won together!

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.750
I won't lose.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:18.790
I must win for Jonouchi and to clear up his misunderstanding of my duel with Pegasus!

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:32.600
Otogi created DDM?

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:37.000
He's battling against Yugi to get revenge for destroying his dreams!

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:41.280
In a short amount of time, Yugi learns the rules and counterattacks.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:46.840
But the dungeon is full of Otogi's monsters, overwhelming Yugi!

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:50.600
For your pride as a duelist, don't lose, Yugi!

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:54.760
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Yugi's Difficult Battle
Orgoth the Relentless's Fierce Attack

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:56.360
Duel, standby!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:07.380
The flask glistens

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:15.230
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:24.200
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:31.980
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:37.810
Shower of happiness

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:41.920
I will shower you with it

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:50.200
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:54.430
Shower of happiness

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:58.560
You are not alone

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:05.280
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
